      {
        "id": 203114,
        "name": "Chaosmancer",
        "username": "Chaosmancer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/{size}/1977_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-09-09T14:51:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"bluedarky\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluedarky/48/1975_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> bluedarky:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Haka pumps himself up before battle, always wears his Ta Moko in battle, and the card text for his battle quotes comes across as loud and boisterous. &nbsp;Whilst it's not impossible for anyone to notice it's him in civilian clothes it's a lot harder than people would think to associate the quiet giant who just showed up and started moving stuff around with the loud and boisterious Haka.As for Legacy in a soup kitchen in Cuba, that would quickly turn into a massive publicity event, Paul Parsons doing the same would be probably be seen as just another do gooder american trying to show off how nice he is.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I hope I'm not coming across as argumenative, but I love back and forths like this.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Haka always has his Ta Moko period. They are tatoos that he took a lot of effort to make, and he does not need to reapply them. But, personality is a lot. He's probably terrifying in combat, which is not how he presents himself out of it. Still, He is unnatural large and has distinctive facial tatoos, there is little hiding who he is, and he doesn't put much effort into trying to hide it. It all depends on how famous Haka is in a given area at the time.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Paul is a completely different story. He is famous. Everyone knows that Paul Parsons is Legacy. His Father and Grandfather were famous in the wars, he's famous, he's married to (if memory serves me) a US Senator. Every aspect of his life leads to him being incredibly well known, and it has been indicated that he has no secret identity. He's never tried to hide who or what he is, so everyone knows it… at least anyone who bothers to pay attention.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:31:59.622Z",
