      {
        "id": 203115,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-09-09T19:03:09.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Also, it's worth noting that in Tactics the public opinion of heroes is rather low. &nbsp;They're no longer being met with parades and confetti. &nbsp;Now, Haka has a lot of practice being disarming with unfriendly/suspicious strangers, so I don't think the negative attitudes will be much of a problem for him. &nbsp;But it means that the towns and villages that he visits are going to be less inclined to brag about his presence.</p>\n<p>And that's even if they can. &nbsp;There are <a href=\"https://www.weforum.org/agenda/2016/05/4-billion-people-still-don-t-have-internet-access-here-s-how-to-connect-them/\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">a lot of people in the world</a> who still don't have internet access. &nbsp;We think of the modern world as having instant communications to every location, but that's not always true in the poorer regions. &nbsp;And that's in <span class=\"bbcode-i\">our</span> world, which hasn't just fought a world-spanning war against the apocalypse. &nbsp;And I think that it's a reasonable bet that those poorer regions are where Haka will be spending most of his time. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>Sure, anyone who really wanted to track Haka down probably could. &nbsp;But the world is still rebuilding from near destruction - everybody has better things to do.</p>",
