      {
        "id": 203116,
        "name": "Medic-Tank",
        "username": "Medic-Tank",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/medic-tank/{size}/2107_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-09-09T21:53:47.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Chaosmancer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/48/1977_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Chaosmancer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I hope I'm not coming across as argumenative, but I love back and forths like this.&nbsp;Haka always has his Ta Moko period. They are tatoos that he took a lot of effort to make, and he does not need to reapply them.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>You might need to revise your lore on that element. This comes from his bio and shows precedent of his Ta Moko disapearing:</p>\n<p><b>However, Aata’s great power is what eventually laid him low, bringing his reign to an end. One morning, after the night of a great battle, his Tā Moko, the facial tattoos identifying him as a Maori warrior, faded completely. Though they knew not what Aata could have done to displease their gods so thoroughly, they took it as a sign that their once great chief had been cursed. Aata’s own right hand man, Ruru, stepped up to challenge him in order to cleanse their village of his taint. Outwitting the giant warrior, still stunned from his tribe turning against him, Ruru dealt Aata a killing blow. Ruru dragged his former friend’s body into the desert, slit his throat, and left him to the dogs.</b></p>\n<p> So it has been clearly established that his immortality can cause it to heal and disapear. He's also shown without it on the picture of the FV BBQ. If I remember well the quote on Ta Moko also supports this. </p>",
