      {
        "id": 203118,
        "name": "Chaosmancer",
        "username": "Chaosmancer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/{size}/1977_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-09-10T04:54:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yeah, what Powerhound said. The Letter's Page told us he only needed to reapply them once, but it was incredibly grueling and painful.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I do agree with Arcanist Lupus, it is still possible to disappear into the world. Like I said, I'm used to considering all the heroes to be super famous, but Haka while recognizable would be one of the less recognizable heroes simply because he's a quiet guy who disappears a lot.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I'm convince that he could have gone off into the mists of the world, tending to the poorest sections of the world during the five years before Tactics starts and even however long it took to get to Prime War.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I am not convinced that is what the actual story is going to be though. There seemed to be hints in the Letters PAge that Haka showing up was a bit more than that.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So, Possible, yes, but I think when we get the story of Haka entering Prime War we are going to be getting a much different story from him.</p>",
