      {
        "id": 203120,
        "name": "Chaosmancer",
        "username": "Chaosmancer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/{size}/1977_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-09-10T17:23:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TakeWalker\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/48/5677_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TakeWalker:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We keep saying \"Well, where could he hide in the world?\" while forgetting this is a world where Atlantis&nbsp;<em>definitely</em> existed. Maybe he got himself stuck in Lemuria, or rocketed to Mars or something.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Well spoilers -&gt; We know in Tactics that the Ennead raised and control Atlantis, clashing with each other as some of them vie for control of the Group. It doesn't feel like Haka is going to be there. The Letters PAge makes it clear that the writers of Sentinel Comics often placed him to solve problems, if he was in Atlantis it would feel like he's meant to solve that and I don't think that is the story of the Ennead, to be solved by Haka.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Plus, the Wagner Mars Base is pretty well known by this point. It's been blown up at least once and people have fought in it multiple times.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>But, I grant that he could be somewhere not on the Earth or even somewhere like the NExus of the Void where really no one goes.</p>",
